# A CC on the auto channel sets a value of the active track as the knob does: AMP HLD by CC 79 and by
# knob B draw the same page. A CC shows no value text, a turn does for a while (over 750 ms on a unit),
# so the two are compared in the graph only (the page's top left).
# Changes the BD track's sound in the active kit and does not put it back.
name: link-cc
state: changes

hold TRK
key BD
release TRK
key AMP
cc 78 0
cc 79 0
cc 80 55
cc 81 0
cc 82 0
cc 83 0
cc 10 64
cc 7 100
cc 79 1
nudge B -1 per 3
wait 750
screen zero
nudge B +42 per 3
wait 750
screen knob
cc 79 0
wait 500
screen back
cc 79 42
wait 500
screen cc
expect knob != zero region 0 9 64 16
expect back == zero region 0 9 64 16
expect cc == knob region 0 9 64 16
cc 79 0
